n(oboInOwl:inSubset obo:CL_4023066 cl:BDS_subset)\n\n  Line 31292: AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:inSubset obo:CL_4023071 cl:BDS_subset)\n\n  Line 31330: AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:inSubset obo:CL_4023075 cl:BDS_subset)\n\n  Line 31345: AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:inSubset obo:CL_4023076 cl:BDS_subset)\n\n  Line 31354: AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:inSubset obo:CL_4023077 cl:BDS_subset)\n\n  Line 31383: AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:inSubset obo:CL_4023080 cl:BDS_subset)\n\n  Line 31394: AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:inSubset obo:CL_4023081 cl:BDS_subset)\n\n  Line 31411: AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:inSubset obo:CL_4023086 cl:BDS_subset)\n\n  Line 31420: AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:inSubset obo:CL_4023087 cl:BDS_subset)\n\n  Line 31428: AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:inSubset obo:CL_4023088 cl:BDS_subset)\n\n  Line 31436: AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:inSubset obo:CL_4023089 cl:BDS_subset)\n\n  Line 31444: AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:inSubset obo:CL_4023090 cl:BDS_subset)\n\n  Line 31452: AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:inSubset obo:CL_4023092 cl:BDS_subset)\n\n  Line 31460: AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:inSubset obo:CL_4023093 cl:BDS_subset)\n\n  Line 31468: AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:inSubset obo:CL_4023094 cl:BDS_subset)\n\n  Line 31476: AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:inSubset obo:CL_4023095 cl:BDS_subset)\n\n  Line 31572: AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:inSubset obo:CL_4023105 cl:BDS_subset)\n\n  Line 31676: AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:inSubset obo:CL_4023118 cl:BDS_subset)\n\n  Line 31691: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:18719084\") rdfs:comment obo:CL_4023119 \"Displaced amacrine cells are a subset of Sox2 expressing amacrine cells.\")\n\n  Line 33598: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:37468586\") rdfs:comment obo:CL_4033092 \"While CD57 is traditionally associated with immune cells (e.g., NK cells), its expression on enterocytes marks unique epithelial subsets with specific functions or maturation states. These cells are specially enriched in areas of the duodenum within submucosal glands.\")\n\n  Line 34190: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:38020069\") rdfs:comment obo:CL_4042036 \"Nearly all melanin-concentrating hormone neurons express the glutamate transporter VGlut2, however a small subset of them expresses the machinery for GABA release and neurotransmission.\")\n\n  Line 34622: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:30270042\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:33916891\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:37495570\") rdfs:comment obo:CL_4052007 \"The S2 fibroblast population has been identified as a subset of intestinal fibroblasts located near the epithelial lining. This population is divided into two subtypes: S2a and S2b. S2a is involved in epithelial differentiation, while S2b, located at the top of the crypt, regulates intestinal stem cell proliferation, niche formation, and wound healing.\")\n\n  Line 34924: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:30904566\") rdfs:comment obo:CL_4052034 \"A thymic tuft cell is a subset of terminally differentiated medullary thymic epithelial cell comprising 5-10% of total mTECs. Lineage-tracing studies indicate that this cell arises from mature MHCII mTECs, with development occurring through both Aire-dependent and Aire-independent pathways. However, its exact origins remain unclear.\")\n\n  Line 35085: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:30429548\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:34512661\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:34857954\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:35784314\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:39198675\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_4052051 \"​​A uterine natural killer subset that is present in the endometrial lining during the non-pregnant state (Garcia-Alonso et al., 2021) and in the decidua during pregnancy (Vento-Tormo et al., 2018). It expresses the uterine resident marker CD49a and is distinguished from uNK2 and uNK3 by CD39 expression and the absence of CD103 (Whettlock et al., 2022) and CD160 (Marečková et al., 2024). It also expresses higher levels of killer-cell immunoglobulin-like receptors (KIRs) and leukocyte immunoglobulin-like receptor B1 (LILRB1), which facilitate interaction with human leukocyte antigens (HLAs) on extravillous trophoblast cells, promoting immune tolerance and implantation. Enriched in the endometrium post-ovulation (Marečková et al., 2024) and prominent in early pregnancy (Whettlock et al., 2022), uNK1 regulates trophoblast invasion and spiral artery remodeling (Zhang & Wei, 2021).\")\n\n  Line 35095: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:30429548\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:34857954\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:35784314\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:39198675\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_4052052 \"A uterine natural killer subset that is present in the endometrial lining during the non-pregnant state (Garcia-Alonso et al., 2021) and in the decidua during pregnancy (Vento-Tormo et al., 2018), peaking in the first trimester. It expresses the uterine resident marker CD49a and is distinguished from uNK1 and uNK3 by the absence of CD39, CD103 (Whettlock et al., 2022), and CD160 (Marečková et al., 2024), with ITGB2 serving as a defining marker (Vento-Tormo et al., 2018). Functionally, it produces more cytokines upon stimulation than uNK1, suggesting a role in immune defense, and secretes XCL1 chemokines, facilitating interactions with maternal dendritic cells and fetal extravillous trophoblasts (Vento-Tormo et al., 2018).\")\n\n  Line 35105: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:30429548\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:31959757\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:34857954\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:35784314\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:39198675\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_4052053 \"A uterine natural killer subset found in the endometrial lining during the non-pregnant state (Garcia-Alonso et al., 2021) and in the decidua during pregnancy (Vento-Tormo et al., 2018), becoming the dominant uNK subset late in pregnancy. It expresses the uterine resident marker CD49a and is distinguished from uNK1 and uNK2 by CD160 (Marečková et al., 2024) and CD103 expression, the absence of CD39, and low KIR levels (Whettlock et al., 2022). Resembling intraepithelial ILC1 cells, uNK3 primarily supports uterine immune defense (Huhn et al., 2020) and indirectly influences trophoblast behavior through chemokine secretion, such as CCL5 (Vento-Tormo et al., 2018).\")\n\n  Line 35490: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:26813785\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:31561945\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:37740916\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_4072015 \"A Kupffer cell located within the hepatic sinusoids, derived from circulating bone marrow monocytes that acquire the phenotypic markers and functional properties of resident Kupffer cells through niche-dependent imprinting, typically following depletion of the embryonically derived Kupffer cell population. During liver injury, MoKCs become the dominant Kupffer cell subset, exhibiting enhanced proliferation, resistance to apoptosis, and key roles in tissue repair and fibrosis attenuation.\")\n\n  Line 35575: AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:inSubset obo:CL_4072027 cl:BDS_subset)\n\n\n(Results truncated: showing 100 of 121 matches (21 hidden). Consider using a more specific path or pattern.)","metadata":{"matches":121,"truncated":true},"title":"subset","time":{"start":1778554055464,"end":1778554055481}},"id":"prt_e1a1518db001xn2Gpvhi51zKMl","sessionID":"ses_1e5ec4b5cffeC1UfvYooVy7sS6","messageID":"msg_e1a14c8c4001rdRCbvF1SdoJ2K"}}
